Question: 1. Why ExecutorService?

Input:
Submit 1,000 tasks while limiting reusable worker threads.

Code:
// Avoid creating one platform thread per task
for (int i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {
    new Thread(task).start();
}

// Prefer managed thread reuse
ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(10);
executor.submit(task);
executor.shutdown();

Output:
The submitted task runs using a worker from the fixed thread pool.

Explanation:
ExecutorService separates task submission from thread management and reuses worker threads.
Always shut down an ExecutorService when it is no longer needed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

